---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const pageTitle = "about";
---
<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
	<p>
		i am currently a master's student studying cybersecurity engineering at washu (in st. louis). 
		i also completed my undergrad at washu, where i majored in computer science. broadly, my research 
		and professional interests lie in creating safe, secure, and robust autonomous systems. i've had the 
		privilege of exploring these interests through my involvement in 
		<a href="https://engineering.washu.edu/faculty/Hussein-Sibai.html" target="_blank">prof. hussein sibai's</a> 
		research group. so far, i've primarily worked on developing novel conformal perception contracts for
		occupancy-based safe planning in closed-loop autonomous driving settings.
	</p>
	<p>
		this summer, i'm working as a software engineering intern at washu's
		<a href="https://di2accelerator.wustl.edu/" target="_blank">di2 accelerator</a>, where i'm helping design and
		deploy the infrastructure for a decentralized agentic network capable of supporting a growing directory of
		autonomous, llm-based agents in coordinating on complex research workflows. part of my work also involves
		implementing new agents and providing an intuitive interface for non-technical users to both interact with and
		contribute their own custom agents to the network.
	</p>
	<p>
		<em>
			i wrote this website in <a href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank">{Astro.generator.toLowerCase()}</a>
			and deployed it on <a href="https://vercel.com/" target="_blank">vercel</a>; it's been both a fun and
			pragmatic way to pick up some web dev skills.
			here's the <a href="https://github.com/amaan-19/website" target="_blank">source code</a> if you're
			interested!
		</em>
	</p>
	<p><em>last updated: june 28 2026</em></p>
</BaseLayout>